Predictive Alert Systems
Prerequisites
Basic Python programming knowledge
Understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with log file formats
Basic understanding of machine learning concepts (classification, training/testing)
Comfortable with package installation using pip
Learning Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Build a machine learning model to predict system alerts from log patterns
Process and extract features from system logs
Train a classification model for alert prediction
Integrate the trained model with live log monitoring
Evaluate model performance and accuracy
Environment Setup
Click the Start Lab button to provision your Linux machine. Once connected via SSH, install the required tools:

# Update package manager
sudo apt update

# Install Python and pip
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv

# Create project directory
mkdir -p ~/predictive-alerts
cd ~/predictive-alerts

# Create virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# Install required packages
pip install scikit-learn pandas numpy
